From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_balloon: larger batches for dense microVM hosts

Stock (and 0001) batching still needs many inflate/deflate round-trips
for large adjustments: with 1024 pfns per batch (4 MiB on 4K pages) a
512 MiB inflate needs 128 tell_host() round-trips, each a synchronous
virtqueue wait.

Push further for hosts that balloon many microVMs at once:

- 1024 -> 2048 pfns per batch (8 MiB per round-trip on 4K pages, 2x
  fewer round-trips; the pfn array grows from 4 KiB to 8 KiB - still
  negligible vs the reclaimed memory).
- OOM deflate 1024 -> 4096 pages (up to 16 MiB freed per OOM event, so
  a spiking guest survives instead of OOM-killing in a loop while the
  host re-inflates).

No behaviour change when the host does not balloon. All virtio feature
bits are untouched.

Tunable: edit the two defines below to taste.

Signed-off-by: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
---
 drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
index 123456789013..123456789022 100644
--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
  * page units.
  */
 #define VIRTIO_BALLOON_PAGES_PER_PAGE (unsigned int)(PAGE_SIZE >> VIRTIO_BALLOON_PFN_SHIFT)
-#define VIRTIO_BALLOON_ARRAY_PFNS_MAX 1024
+#define VIRTIO_BALLOON_ARRAY_PFNS_MAX 2048
 /* Maximum number of (4k) pages to deflate on OOM notifications. */
-#define VIRTIO_BALLOON_OOM_NR_PAGES 1024
+#define VIRTIO_BALLOON_OOM_NR_PAGES 4096
 #define VIRTIO_BALLOON_OOM_NOTIFY_PRIORITY 80
